{title: I Will Sing of My Redeemer}
{artist: Philip P. Bliss / James McGranahan}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 9/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Crusade Songs, edited by W. Hines Sims (Nashville, Tennessee: Broadman Press, 1954), # 20)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I will sing of my Re[D7]deemer,
[D7]And His wondrous love to [G]me;
[G]On the cruel cross He [D7]suffered,
[D7]From the curse to set me [G]free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Sing, oh [C]sing, of my Re[G]deemer,
[G]With His [D7]blood, He purchased [G]me.
[G]On the cross,__[C]__ He sealed my par__[G]__don,
[G]Paid the debt, and made me free.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I will tell the wondrous [D7]story,
[D7]How my lost estate to [G]save,
[G]In His boundless love and [D7]mercy,
[D7]He the ransom freely [G]gave.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I will praise my dear Re[D7]deemer,
[D7]His triumphant power I’ll [G]tell,
[G]How the victory He [D7]giveth
[D7]Over sin, and death, and [G]hell.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]I will sing of my Re[D7]deemer,
[D7]And His heav’nly love to [G]me;
[G]He from death to life hath [D7]brought me,
[D7]Son of God with Him to [G]be.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
